      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-1,5],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-1$ and $b=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(5-(-1))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{36}{12}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{3}≈1.732.\n$$",
